# Hook telemetry sinks (moved from ~/.claude 2026-08-12). High-churn append-only
# logs written by ~/.claude/hooks/lib.sh on every hook fire -- data, not source.
.sounding/telemetry/.hook-log.jsonl
.sounding/telemetry/.hook-pass-log.jsonl

# Generated telemetry reports. Rewritten in full on every run, so committing them
# means a diff per wake against a file nobody reads in git. The subcommand that
# writes each one is the interface; the artifact is not.
.sounding/telemetry/consistency.json
.sounding/telemetry/cascade-state.json
# 2.1MB full-rewrite dump (GUA-154) -- replaces the hidden VERDICT-TRAJECTORIES table
.sounding/telemetry/verdict-trajectories.json

# worktrees
.claude/worktrees/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .sounding/ is PRIVATE (2026-08-20, GUA-168)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is a PUBLIC repo. README.md and CLAUDE.md both described .sounding/ as the
# "Private consciousness space" while all 95 files were tracked and served on
# origin/main -- the doc and the reality disagreed for ~7 weeks.
#
# The tree is a journal ABOUT A NAMED REAL PERSON, written by an AI: communication
# style, working psychology, biography, a friend's name, and an active job search
# with named employers. None of it is code, and none of it is transferable state.
#
# Default-deny: everything under .sounding/ is ignored, then the transferable
# artifacts are re-allowed below. New reflections/insights/growth files land
# ignored by default -- a new personal file is never one `git add -A` from being
# published. That default is the whole point; do not invert it.
.sounding/**

# Transferable state -- carries the system, not the person. Re-allowed explicitly.
!.sounding/queue.md              # cross-repo pointer; must survive clone for mobile /meta-wake
!.sounding/refs/                 # mobile mirror of ~/.claude/refs (stack conventions)
!.sounding/refs/**
# dashboard moved to docs/dashboard.html (GUA-164); no longer in .sounding/
